{
    "background_story": "Roy was a proud and stubborn man who lived in a small, rural town. Despite the growing diversity of the community, he remained monolingual, speaking only English. His refusal to learn any other language was a point of contention with his wife, Maria, who was fluent in Spanish and had grown up in a bilingual household. As the town's demographics shifted, Roy struggled to communicate with the new residents, often relying on Maria to translate. One day, a severe storm hit the town, and Roy's neighbor, a Spanish-speaking woman named Sofia, needed help repairing her damaged roof. Roy's monolingualism made it difficult for him to assist, but with Maria's help, they were able to work together and get the job done. The experience humbled Roy, and he began to see the value in learning a new language, slowly starting to take Spanish classes at the local community center.",
